From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hipuu <hipuu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mm/mglru: default lru_gen_min_ttl to 1000 ms

The MGLRU kernel documentation (Documentation/admin-guide/mm/multigen_lru.rst)
recommends N=1000 ms to protect the working set from being evicted under
reclaim pressure, "based on the average human detectable lag (~100ms)". The
kernel default is 0, which lets kswapd evict pages of the current working
set the moment memory pressure appears — the refault storm that follows
burns CPU (zram decompression) and flash I/O both. The fork's
workingset/refault fixes reduce the damage but the working set is still
unprotected by default.

There is no Kconfig symbol for this value and no boot hook in this
pipeline, so set the compile-time default. Runtime override stays
available: write 0 to /sys/kernel/mm/lru_gen/min_ttl_ms.

Context is identical in both common bases (Hipuu 6.6.142 fork and
OnePlusOSS 6.6.118); the change only takes effect under CONFIG_LRU_GEN
(enabled in both).
---
 mm/vmscan.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/vmscan.c b/mm/vmscan.c
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -5018 +5018 @@
-static unsigned long lru_gen_min_ttl __read_mostly;
+static unsigned long lru_gen_min_ttl __read_mostly = msecs_to_jiffies(1000);
